Backlog tail, Selected item/items:
1. Detach keyboard-bar from `/api/char`; handle domain selection locally, use `/api/render-prompt` for prompt resolution
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/api-client.js': Add `renderPrompt(domain, prompt)` POST method
        - new async method that POSTs to `/api/render-prompt` with `{ domain, prompt }` body
        - returns parsed JSON (`{ text, lines, chars }`)
        - `sendChar` stays in the file (unchanged) but is no longer called by keyboard-bar
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/keyboard-bar.js': Refactor to track domains locally; split key handling into domain-local vs prompt-remote
        - add `#sharedDomains`, `#pudDomains`, `#selectedDomain` state
        - add public `setDomains(shared, pud)` method to receive boot data
        - add `#onDomainKey(key)`: pure local mutation — set `#selectedDomain`, update all button states (highlighted / active / inactive), set prompt button labels from `domain.prompts`, no API call
        - add `#onPromptKey(key)`: look up `#selectedDomain.prompts[i]` by position, call `apiClient.renderPrompt(domain, prompt)`, on success set `#stagedPrompt` and highlight the pressed button
        - `#handleKeydown` and button click handlers route to `#onDomainKey` / `#onPromptKey` instead of the old `#onButtonClick` → `sendChar`
        - `#formatStatus` simplified: domain status is set inline (no `result_type` from API); prompt status uses the `renderPrompt` response fields (`text`, `lines`, `chars`)
        - Enter / Ctrl+Enter behaviour unchanged (still dispatch `prompt-fired` / copy `#stagedPrompt`)
        - button state classes (`kb-active`, `kb-highlighted`, `kb-inactive`) driven entirely by local state, not by a backend response
    [ ] 'content/web-ui/frontend/clanker-app.js': Pass boot domain data into keyboard-bar after successful boot
        - in `#bootSystem()`, after `apiClient.boot()` succeeds, call `this.#keyboardBar.setDomains(boot.shared_domains, boot.pud_domains)`
        - no other changes to clanker-app

No backend changes needed — `/api/render-prompt` already accepts the `{ domain, prompt }` shape and `deserialize_domain_prompt` handles it. `/api/char` remains available but is simply no longer called from the UI.
