VI. finished stuffs

1. Merge `ManifestResolver` into `RepoContentResolver` — two nullable PUD filesets, content-over-metadata overlap
    [x] `content/backend/core/core/entities.py`: Remove `ManifestResolver` class; rework `RepoContentResolver` to carry `content_fileset: PudFileset | None` and `meta_fileset: PudFileset | None`; add `FILE_META_UL` / `FILE_META_CLOSE` delimiter pair for the single-line metadata tag
        - `content_fileset` produces full-content blocks (existing `READ_FILESET` delims)
        - `meta_fileset` produces line-count metadata blocks (new delims, format: `<file_meta path="…" loc=N/>`)
        - files present in both sets are emitted in content only, removed from metadata
        - content blocks precede metadata blocks in output
        - drop `SharedFileset` from the resolver entirely (shared-manifest capability is gone)
    [x] `content/backend/render_pipeline/render_service.py`: Absorb `_res_manifest` and `_build_manifest` into `_res_repo_content`; add overlap subtraction (`B - A`); emit content blocks then metadata blocks; drop `ManifestResolver` from `TYPE_ORDER` and from `_dispatch` match arms
        - `_res_repo_content` resolves `content_fileset` → full blocks, `meta_fileset` → metadata blocks, applies `meta_paths -= content_paths`
        - `_dispatch` match loses the `ManifestResolver` case
        - `TYPE_ORDER` shrinks to `[RepoContentResolver, MultiDocResolver]`
    [x] `content/backend/asset_ingestion/extractors/map_extractor2.py`: Simplify `RepoContentResParser.preprocess` to identity `return data` (both filesets are now explicit named keys in the config dict)
        - no longer needs the `if "fileset" in data` guard or the wrap-and-pop pattern
    (the user will update yaml of existing RepoContentResolver to declare 'content_fileset' rather than 'fileset')

